meta {
  name: update-item
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/menu/items/{{admin_item_uid}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "price_minor": 19000,
    "is_bestseller": true
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })

  test("the new price does not touch orders already placed", function () {
    // order_item snapshots name and unit price at order time (docs/DECISIONS.md D8). Verify by
    // re-running admin-orders / get-order afterwards: its totals are unchanged.
    expect(res.body.data.price.minor).to.equal(19000)
  })
}

docs {
  # Update a menu item

Raising a price here is the case `order_item`'s snapshotting exists for. Run
`admin-orders / get-order` afterwards and confirm the earlier order's total has not moved.

**`image_url` is special on this route.** Supplying it also clears any uploaded photo
(`image_key`), because the two are one field to a client and the uploaded copy takes precedence
(docs/DECISIONS.md D15). Without that, pasting a URL over an uploaded photo would answer 200 and
change nothing visible. `"image_url": ""` clears the dish's photo whichever way it was set.
}
